**"Software"** means the MeetingBot source code, object code, documentation, configuration, and any accompanying files distributed under this license.

**"Derivative Work"** means any work based on or incorporating the Software, including a modified, translated, adapted, or repackaged version of the Software.

**"Output"** means content, text, code, designs, documents, or other material generated by a user through use of the Software. Output does not include the Software itself or a Derivative Work.

**"Resale"** means selling, renting, leasing, licensing, sublicensing, or otherwise distributing the Software or a Derivative Work for a fee, or repackaging the Software or a Derivative Work with changes that are primarily cosmetic or otherwise do not add substantial independent value, for the purpose of selling that repackaged software. Resale includes distributing the Software or a Derivative Work as a standalone product, or as a primary component of a product or service whose value is substantially the Software itself.

**"Enterprise Use"** means use by a company, organization, team, or individual for internal business purposes, client projects, commercial projects, or other revenue-generating work, where the Software is used as a tool to produce Output or to support the user's own work, rather than being resold as the Software.

